## F4: macOS run-only mode
State: todo
Description: On Darwin, `./andes-sim run` re-execs inside a prebuilt Linux
runtime image (qemu-system-riscv64 + sim_* engines + plugin + runtime libs)
in the podman machine VM. Hard rule: the mmap file stays VM-local (container
/dev/shm with --shm-size=3g, or a named volume) -- NEVER a virtiofs bind-mount
of a host dir (crosses kernels, breaks coherency). The repo/ELF bind-mount is
fine (plain file I/O). The F1 resolver works unchanged inside the container.
Two halves:
  a) runtime image: Dockerfile target that copies build artifacts (built on
     Linux CI); publish registry/name is an open question for the PM.
  b) driver/wrapper: Darwin detection + podman invocation + UX (pull hint).
Apple Silicon runs the x86-64 image under emulation; an arm64 image is a
later optimization, out of scope here.
Key files: andes-sim (wrapper), scripts/ (new run-in-container helper),
verilator/Dockerfile or a new root Dockerfile.runtime
Dependencies: F1; Linux CI image publishing (external)

## F5: model-neutral --mem-size flag
State: todo
Description: One flag on `run` lets the user request guest memory for every
model:
  --mem-size SPEC   (SPEC = 256M, 1.5G, 2G, raw bytes -- reuses parse_size)
  - model=hybrid: same path as --mmap-size today (mem size == mmap size ==
    QEMU backend size == vsim RAM window).
  - model=fast: QEMU as-is. Flag absent -> argv untouched (no -m, no mmap
    file, no shm resolver; QEMU applies its own defaults). Flag given ->
    append plain `-m SPEC` and let QEMU validate it (it already errors
    clearly above the 2 GiB DRAM window). Never memory-backend-file here.
  - model=cycle: validate only; vsim standalone always models the full
    0x0..0x8FFFFFFF window, nothing to size.
Early >2G validation in the driver applies to hybrid only (there a bad size
would allocate a huge mmap file before QEMU dies late). `--mmap-size` stays
as a hidden alias (parity golden hsim.py, existing notebooks/tests); docs
teach only --mem-size.
Key files: driver/cli.cpp, driver/cmd_run.cpp, driver/engine_registry.cpp
(standalone template), driver/run_plan.cpp, driver/cli_test.cpp,
driver/plan_test.cpp, tests/andes_sim/ (fast-model -m smoke)
Dependencies: none (F2's 2G e2e test should use this flag once both exist)

